Roman: Last Case of the Day, Detective
Roman: Make your decision
Detective: It's...
do can_click_now()

- Maya Deren, The Artist
	After accusing Miss Deren to be the culprit, the tattooing incidents continued significantly.
	Due to the continuous slaughter of her reputation, Miss Deren has closed her shop for the meantime and has gone somewhere else to devote her creativity passions.
	do InterviewTracker.romanFail(true)
- Mona Vale, The Social Media Coordinator
	After accusing Mona Vale to be the culprit, Mona Vale confessed immediately due to the pressure.
	She revealed that she wanted to become an artist like Maya Deren, but could not due to the constant judgment from Miss Deren.
	“Using what I knew about Miss Deren and the letters that Adelaide had sent us, I wanted to set up Miss Deren in order to ensure she could never judge others’ art ever again!!”  
- Adelaide, The Protestor
	After Adelaide’s arrest, public outrage grew over the “religious extremist” suspect.
	However, new victims appeared while she remained in custody, disproving her involvement.
	Handwriting analysis later linked all threatening letters to another source.
	Adelaide was released and cleared of all charges, though her reputation suffered permanent damage.
	do InterviewTracker.romanFail(true)
do go_to_next_crime()
=> END